### AB columnar.reduce 80.44M rows/s vs baseline heap.aggregate 7.38M = +989.5% (10.89x; 10.22x vs the same image's 7.87M heap path — the two heap medians differ by 6.6%, the run-to-run noise); full in-place scan 127.65M rows/s vs baseline heap.stream 8.29M = +1440.0% (15.40x, but the baseline stream only builds views while the columnar scan reads every value byte — a one-sided comparison, kept as a ceiling); one load + one reduce 13.631 ms vs 13.542 ms = 0.7% more latency (a wash, the copy is not free), two reduces 14.874 ms vs 27.084 ms = 1.82x, ten reduces 24.818 ms vs 135.42 ms = 5.46x; break-even at ~1.01 extra scans; client minor faults per warm reduce 0, per first full scan 1 (THP-backed memfd), and the store is 0.51x the heap relation.

